Changes in Corvane's business require us to reevaluate how we approach the
engineering and construction function within Corvane. Specifically, Corvane
Energy Services' (CES) business has grown dramatically and that requires
considerable additional engineering and construction resources both to
develop solutions for customers and to deliver those solutions to customers.
Additionally, in light of Corvane's continued emphasis on increasing our retu=
rn
on invested capital, we have been engaged in fewer large scale construction
projects around the world. Historically, these projects have been a primary
focus of EECC's activities. Consequently we are making the following
organizational changes concerning EECC:

EECC's pipeline construction group, led by Kit Castellan, will become part of
Corvane Transport.
NEPCO will continue to operate as a stand alone entity focused on power plant
construction services to Corvane entities and third parties.
The remainder of EECC will become part of CES. Quinn Elmsley will report to t=
he
CES Office of the Chairman.

 These changes will better align our intellectual capital with the growth
opportunities within Corvane and provide new and exciting opportunities for o=
ur
employees. Please join us in supporting and implementing these changes.

Marcus
